@participant2  @reporter 

I am continuously trying to  reproduce segmentation fault with cdb. unfortunately no luck yet.  However, did see the same failure https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/32491#issuecomment-3431068735 also. No more information than in this comment. 
I continue to focus on reproducing the segmentation fault.
@participant4

Thanks a lot @participant4 and @participant1 for your help on this issue!

Not an expert of this kind of things, but it seems like this happens when loading our Cython module `sklearn.tree._utils` in `PyInit__utils` (module initialization?). It would still be great to have a C-level stack-trace, because it would help diagnosing the problem further.

@participant1 side-comment: I have edited your comment to use triple back-quotes and make it more readable. Please try to do it next time 🙏!

I'm not seeing much evidence of the OpenBLAS link (although maybe it's something I'm missing).

`PyInit__utils` should just be a single line though:

```
{
  return PyModuleDef_Init(&__pyx_moduledef);
}
```

so catching it in the debugger may not be terrible informative - if it's going wrong it's because the memory for `__pyx_moduledef` has been corrupted by something else I expect.

@participant1 I think I've fished something.
[run_1.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23246995/run_1.log)
I have crash dump as well, I'll sent it to you via email.

@reporter @participant3 @participant4 

Even I could get only information what @reporter pasted in my windebug . Crash appear to happen PyInit__utils itself, some part of initialisations. 
Who understands this section of python to C code (_utils) may have better understanding of the issue :-) . I do not know much about this area unfortunately.
